t 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5d98bf002045c2b15175608d93dbbb4c39ce98be181537fea0afc1609a1ed426","compact":"34c25e6e1fa2140ae26fe6402c04e7b1579fde241ab48edf069ed3476ee23f2a","nasal":"18485c4d4c15fadf75eccefbca44c6724675b9e6a3857ac27bd3f07ee305bbf7"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-35-30","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":35,"verse":30,"english":"Considering that he was a mere child and therefore not tarnished by any sin and that a great divine work would be accomplished by him in future the sun did not burn Hanuman.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.737,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-35-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7035030","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"815423ea073a9bdafaec34b3d623100812b8447a111902c3a23f9193426f781c","compact":"188f2a9a35318645d1c76a92c4e20db81afb171894736dedb954755d770acdbe","nasal":"188f2a9a35318645d1c76a92c4e20db81afb171894736dedb954755d770acdbe"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-35-31","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":35,"verse":31,"english":"At the every day when Hanuman sprang up to hold the sun, Rāhu too essayed to possess him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-35-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7035031","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dbffaa2b738e66205578822db6852b273bebd86e489b1f596d7704f72d6d79cc","compact":"6ca849a2e6d838fe73b15cea4684d98e81e2bd9b2e665c13d14e85dad6cb9bff","nasal":"6ca849a2e6d838fe73b15cea4684d98e81e2bd9b2e665c13d14e85dad6cb9bff"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-35-32","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":35,"verse":32,"english":"Having reached the top of the sun's car Hanuman touched Rāhu; so he, the repressor of the moon's rays, accordingly went back on beholding the sun thus possessed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttR